{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1011957-queries-ananasi-pentex","id":1011957,"title":"Queries (Ananasi, Pentex)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-04T05:33:09-08:00","id":1011957,"title":"Queries (Ananasi, Pentex)","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> In the middle of a chronicle, and would like your views and anything you can glean about the default position on these queries:<br /> <br /> 1) How much does Pentex know about other shifters, and how widespread is that knowledge within the organization? Does it distribute on a 'need to know' basis, is it regionally distributed based on how much of a threat they assess each shifter to be in different sites, is there a department that gathers and/or controls this information? Or is all this left vague for ST?<br /> <br /> 2) Ananasi in Crawlerling form (and some Camazotz) must assign Leaders to head the collective mind. If these leaders are terminated, the reformed Ananasi loses a % of its memories, depending on how many Leaders there were. So, dividing into 100 spiders and assigning 9 spiders to each of 10 Leaders means that for every Leader that dies, a 10% loss of memory occurs when reforming. Implicit in this of course is the notion that Ananasi can reform when there are missing Leaders. So my query is, can Ananasi do this at will, so that they can leave some of their Crawlerling form behind and reform with partial memories, or is the conscious order to reform fully collective i.e. all spiders left MUST reform when the call is made? If the latter, wouldn't a selective reform be a cool Gift or Merit, and what level/cost and type would you assign that Gift/Merit?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any insight and input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-04-2016, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:59:36-08:00","id":1012049,"title":"","content":"It would be a Merit if they could store their memories in a living spider for latter recall (allowing them to provide lie perfectly about events because they would literally have no memory of the event). The drawback would be that the memories are lost if the living spider is killed and that other Ananasi could gain the memories by consuming the living spider. I would charge 1 point for that Merit because of its limited utility and potential drawbacks.<br /> <br /> As for Pentex, they have imperfect knowledge of the Garou (the BSD are only willing to share so much and, in their madness, most of what they share is incorrect). For example, I could see a BSD that was deathly afraid of chocolate (a derangement) telling its Pentex allies that all Garou are deathly afraid of chocolate because it is a lethal toxin to canines. Any sane Garou who encountered fomori armed with chocolate bars would be very confused after the fight, especially when the first round consisted of fomori confidently chucking Hershey bars at the Garou in order to paralyze them with fear. I imagine that their information about other Fera is even less reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:17:47-08:00","id":1012058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1011957-queries-ananasi-pentex?p=1012049#post1012049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Pentex, they have imperfect knowledge of the Garou (the BSD are only willing to share so much and, in their madness, most of what they share is incorrect). For example, I could see a BSD that was deathly afraid of chocolate (a derangement) telling its Pentex allies that all Garou are deathly afraid of chocolate because it is a lethal toxin to canines. Any sane Garou who encountered fomori armed with chocolate bars would be very confused after the fight, especially when the first round consisted of fomori confidently chucking Hershey bars at the Garou in order to paralyze them with fear. I imagine that their information about other Fera is even less reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very tempted to have a coco tossing first team at some point...just water balloons full of chocolate milk!<br /> <br /> Anywho, I agree that Pentex is not all knowing, especially in regards to the Fera, since they are supposed to be rather rare. I can see in the Amazon some knowledge of Bastet and Mokole (due to actual interaction), but even then I'm sure they wouldn't know things like Mokole being allergic to gold (since silver works so well anyway). BUT I do want to say remember how expensive gold is, should Corax or Mokole come up in your campaign. From a quick google its $1,179.79 per oz....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 12-04-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:27:13-08:00","id":1012079,"title":"","content":"In a game I ran in which a player was playing an Ananasi this scenario basically came up. The character switched into Crawlerling form but two his leaders ended up getting trapped by the enemy, so when the character reassumed her normal form she was missing a large chunk of her memories. <br /> <br /> I decided that she had 24 hours to go back and recapture her leaders to regain her memories. After 24 hours the memories stored in those spiders would quickly begin degrading, the spiders would turn into normal spiders and the memories would be lost forever. <br /> <br /> As for a merit for storing memories - I wouldn't make it more than 2 dots at maximum. It doesn't seem like it would be terribly handy in most situations. At the very least keep in mind the 7 dot merit, Hive Mind which essentially allows all of your spiders to hold all of your memories, so if even one survives you won't lose anything. <br /> <br /> For the Pentex situation I assume that Strike Teams are generally familiar with some basic knowledge about supernatural beings and probably have a general understanding of their weaknesses. Members probably know werewolves are vulnerable to silver and vampires don't like sunlight. They would probably have never heard of more esoteric creatures (Ananasi, Rokea, Nagah, Mokole) or their weaknesses, though perhaps a few Teams in specific locations might be more familiar with them (First Teams in the Amazon are probably somewhat familiar with Mokole and some Bastest breeds for example).<br /> <br /> Past that though, the vast majority of Pentex workers are just regular folks who would scoff at the ideas of vampires or werewolves existing. Even in certain more supernatural-focuseds subgroups like Project Iliad and Odyssey, most of the rank and file members probably don't <i>really</i> believe in werewolves or vampires until they've encountered such things themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:33:58-08:00","id":1012082,"title":"","content":"I can't chime in on Ananasi, but as for Pentex... They are literally making their own breeds of Fera. They have powerful, ancient spirit and Spiral allies, along with vampire elders. I would never call their knowledge &quot;complete&quot;, especially on issues such as politics and culture... But I would certainly assume they have a strong grasp of basic Werewolf mechanics and a gist of their most common gifts and fetishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:13:21-08:00","id":1012095,"title":"","content":"Thank you these are helpful comments. Do we think that Pentex is really that clueless about the Fera though? They do seem to have some corrupted or fallen shifters (see Book of Wyrm 20) among their ranks. Would an Ananasi caught on recordings be recognised for what it is? I guess what I'm wondering is, does the ultra conspiratorial and cutthroat subculture of Pentex view such knowledge as an important edge in being upwardly mobile and so individuals guard it jealously from work rivals? Resulting in a terribly exploitable weakness few Fera are clued in on?<br /> Also AnubusXy, I really like your idea. It adds tensions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-04-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:16:23-08:00","id":1012123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1011957-queries-ananasi-pentex?p=1012082#post1012082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't chime in on Ananasi, but as for Pentex... They are literally making their own breeds of Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>By trial and error with forces they don't fully comprehend, doing shit that they've guessed might do something. And the results are typically about as high in quality as one might assume they would be given the slapdash nature of such efforts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have powerful, ancient spirit and Spiral allies </div> </div> </div>Allies is stretching it. They have occasional werewolf freelancers, and most of them probably aren't super high ranking. The rest of the tribe is not nearly so cooperative. As for spirits, the subsidiaries are mostly human, and as far as Werewolf is concerned, humans don't usually do a good job of communicating or holding sway over spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> along with vampire elders </div> </div> </div>Two of them. Who don't have super-deep knowledge of Garou or Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would never call their knowledge &quot;complete&quot;, especially on issues such as politics and culture... But I would certainly assume they have a strong grasp of basic Werewolf mechanics and a gist of their most common gifts and fetishes. </div> </div> </div>Maybe even less than that. Even subsidiary employees who are in the know aren't too well-informed about their own shadowy corners, much less the ones that want them dead and don't tend to explain why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:00:41-08:00","id":1012155,"title":"","content":"Remember that Pentex is afflicted with the worst aspects of corporate culture and corporate politics. Divisions do not share information with other divisions and managers do not share information with their inferiors, their peers, or their superiors. Everyone is looking for an edge for promotions and raises and, if that means looking the other way while Garou shred a competing division, so be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T03:51:43-08:00","id":1013672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1011957-queries-ananasi-pentex?p=1012155#post1012155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Pentex is afflicted with the worst aspects of corporate culture and corporate politics. Divisions do not share information with other divisions and managers do not share information with their inferiors, their peers, or their superiors. Everyone is looking for an edge for promotions and raises and, if that means looking the other way while Garou shred a competing division, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Pentex is huge and ran by self serving bastards. Just because some of them have knowledge they should not does not mean the company as a whole has a manual for dealing with all threats that looks like it was cribbed from the WW books. After all even some of their most dangerous members and teams are misinformed and work under false assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:35:47-08:00","id":1013749,"title":"","content":"In addition, not every division of Pentex is Evil with a capital 'E'. Some of them are normal corporations (evil with a small 'e') that just exist to make Pentex money. Some of them are charitable enterprises operated by good people that are used by Pentex to gather information or to generate tax deductions that they can channel to other divisions. <br /> <br /> For example, Pentex might maintain a division that runs a group of non-profit health clinics that give free medical service to impoverished areas in the USA. Access to the medical records of the patients allows Pentex to determine the exact amount of physiological and psychological damage that their other divisions are doing to the local population and, with that information, Pentex can more accurately adjust their practices to maximize human suffering. Access to the medical records also allows Pentex to maintain a massive list of potential organ and tissue 'donors' and, on occasion, the organ harvesting organization that Pentex controls grabs patients from their homes when there are wealthy enough individuals willing to pay enough money for their organs. In addition, Pentex generates tax deductions for other divisions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:03:12-08:00","id":1013968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1011957-queries-ananasi-pentex?p=1013749#post1013749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, not every division of Pentex is Evil with a capital 'E'. Some of them are normal corporations (evil with a small 'e')<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, a lot of real world corporations use the capital letter. Conflict diamonds, covering up hexavalent chromium in the water so they don't have to pay fines... it's shitbag city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}